    "media:imagetext": "BRACE POSITION\nWHEN SO DIRECTED, ASSUME THIS POSITION BEFORE AND\nDURING LANDING. WITH SEAT BELT FASTENED, PLACE BOTH FEET\nTOGETHER ON THE FLOOR IN FRONT OF YOU, LEAN FORWARD\nAND DOWN AS FAR AS POSSIBLE AND CLASP HANDS FIRMLY\nUNDER LEGS\nWhere time permits, flight attendant will pass out blankets and pillows for padding.\nA word about Seats and Seat Belts\nTHE \"FASTEN SEAT BELT\"\nSIGN IS LOCATED DIRECTLY ABOVE THE CABIN ENTRANCE AT THE FORWARD END OF THE CABIN. ROUGH AIR\n(TURBULENCE) AT HIGH ALTITUDES, ALTHOUGH INFREQUENT, CAN BE SEVERE. WHEN THE SEAT BELT SIGN IS ILLUMINATED IN-FLIGHT,\nPLEASE COMPLY WITH THE SIGN TO PREVENT POSSIBLE INJURY. SEASONED AIR TRAVELERS USUALLY LEAVE THIER SEAT BELTS FASTENED\nALL THE TIME AND PULL THEM SNUG WHENEVER THE SEAT BELT SIGN IS LIGHTED.\nOxygen\nFLOTATION CUSHION\nOXYGEN IS AVAILABLE FOR MEDICAL PURPOSES, SHOULD THE NEED ARISE.\nFloatation Seat Cushions\nYOUR SEAT CUSHION IS A LIFE PRESERVER. IN THE EVENT OF EMERGENCY DITCHING ON\nWATER, GRASP THE BACK OF THE CUSHION AND PULL UPWARD TO REMOVE. HOLD TIGHTLY TO\nYOUR CHEST WITH ARMS THROUGH THE STRAPS. TAKE IT WITH YOU.\nSmoking\nTHE \"No-SMOKING\" SIGN IS LOCATED DIRECTLY ABOVE THE CABIN ENTRANCE AT THE FORWARD END OF THE CABIN. WHEN THE SIGN\nIS OFF, YOU MAY SMOKE WHILE SEATED IN A SMOKING AREA OF THE CABIN. WHEN THE SIGN IS ILLUMINATED, HOWEVER, SMOKING\nWILL NOT BE PERMITTED.\nPets in the Cabin\nA PET BEING TRANSPORTED MUST REMAIN IN ITS KENNEL AND THE KENNEL MUST REMAIN IN THE CARRY-ON LUGGAGE RACK OR STOWED\nSAFELY BENEATH A PASSENGER SEAT. THIS SERVICE IS ON A SPACE AVAILABLE BASIS ONLY.\nFEDERAL REGULATIONS\nSeat Backs and Seat Trays\nEACH PASSENGER SEAT BACK AND SEAT TRAY MUST BE IN AN UPRIGHT POSITION PRIOR TO TAXIING,\nTAKE-OFF OR LANDING.\nEACH PASSENGER MUST COMPLY WITH INSTRUCTIONS GIVEN BY CREW MEMBERS IN COMPLIANCE WITH THIS REGULATION,\nAlcoholic Beverages\nNO PERSON SHALL DRINK ANY ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGE ABOARD AN AIR CARRIER UNLESS SUCH BEVERAGE HAS BEEN SERVED TO\nHIM/HER BY THE AIR CARRIER OPERATING THE AIRCRAFT.\nNO AIR CARRIER SHALL SERVE ANY ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGE TO ANY PERSON ABOARD AN AIR CARRIER AIRCRAFT IF SUCH PERSON\nAPPEARS TO BE INTOXICATED,\nNO AIR CARRIER SHALL PERMIT ANY PERSON TO BOARD AN AIR CARRIER AIRCRAFT IF SUCH PERSON APPEARS TO BE INTOXICATED.\nALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES CANNOT BE SERVED TO MINORS.\nALL GLASSES AND CANS MUST BE REMOVED FROM CABIN BEFORE LANDING.\nCarry-on Baggage\nCARRY-ON BAGGAGE IS LIMITED TO AN AMOUNT THAT CAN BE PLACED BENEATH THE SEAT, WITH THE EXCEPTION OF HANG-UP\nBAGS WHICH MAY BE HUNG IN THE CLOSET, AND COATS AND HATS WHICH MAY BE PLACED IN THE OVERHEAD RACK.\nALL CARRY-ON RETAINED BY THE PASSENGER MUST BE PLACED BENEATH THE SEAT DURING TAKE-OFF AND LANDING.\nNo-Smoking Section\nPROVIDED FOR EACH PERSON DESIRING A SEAT IN THE NO-SMOKING SECTION, IT IS FREQUENTLY NECESSARY\nTO EXPAND THE NO-SMOKING SECTION TO ACCOMMODATE EVERYONE. IN THE EVENT OF A FULL FLIGHT IT IS, SOMETIMES,\nNECESSARY TO SEAT SMOKERS IN THE REMAINING SEATS OF THE LAST NO-SMOKING ROW. SMOKING\nIS PROHIBITED IN ALL\nROWS PERMANENTLY OR TEMPORARILY DESIGNATED \"No-SMOKING\".\nRV 4/83\nDO NOT TAKE THIS CARD FROM THE AIRCRAFT",
